{"schemaVersion":1,"catalog":"english","dataset":"tests","sheet":"14 - Tests","table":"TestsTable","updatedAt":"2026-08-01T00:00:00Z","recordCount":120,"records":[{"ID":"T1-01","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"Had we identified the dependency earlier, we ___ the outage.","A":"would prevent","B":"would have prevented","C":"prevented","D":"had prevented","Source ID":"D-001"},{"ID":"T1-02","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"The evidence must be retained, ___ the project is terminated early.","A":"whether","B":"even if","C":"unless","D":"provided","Source ID":"D-002"},{"ID":"T1-03","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"No sooner ___ the patch deployed than a new indicator appeared.","A":"was","B":"had we","C":"we had","D":"did we","Source ID":"D-003"},{"ID":"T1-04","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"The design is robust, ___ somewhat costly to operate.","A":"although","B":"albeit","C":"despite","D":"however","Source ID":"D-004"},{"ID":"T1-05","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"It is essential that every exception ___ by the risk owner.","A":"is approved","B":"be approved","C":"will be approved","D":"has approved","Source ID":"D-005"},{"ID":"T1-06","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Business","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"I would rather the supplier ___ the limitation before the demo.","A":"disclosed","B":"had disclosed","C":"would disclose","D":"has disclosed","Source ID":"D-006"},{"ID":"T1-07","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Business","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"Only after the rollback ___ stable again.","A":"the service became","B":"did the service become","C":"became the service","D":"the service did become","Source ID":"D-007"},{"ID":"T1-08","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Business","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"The control is designed to prevent data ___ outside the region.","A":"to transfer","B":"from being transferred","C":"being transferring","D":"to be transfer","Source ID":"D-008"},{"ID":"T1-09","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Business","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"By Q4, we ___ the legacy identity provider.","A":"will retire","B":"will have retired","C":"retired","D":"have retired","Source ID":"D-009"},{"ID":"T1-10","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Business","Skill":"Grammar","Level":"C1","Question":"Were the vendor ___ the clause, we could proceed.","A":"accept","B":"to accept","C":"accepted","D":"accepting","Source ID":"D-010"},{"ID":"T1-11","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Vocabulary","Level":"C1","Question":"Which phrase most clearly means “a problem that stops the whole programme”?","A":"a minor caveat","B":"a single point of failure","C":"a stretch goal","D":"a quick win","Source ID":"D-011"},{"ID":"T1-12","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Vocabulary","Level":"C1","Question":"“We need to iron out the remaining issues” means:","A":"hide them","B":"resolve small difficulties","C":"escalate immediately","D":"cancel the work","Source ID":"D-012"},{"ID":"T1-13","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Vocabulary","Level":"C1","Question":"A “trade-off” is:","A":"a contractual penalty","B":"a balance between competing benefits","C":"a staffing change","D":"an accounting error","Source ID":"D-013"},{"ID":"T1-14","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Vocabulary","Level":"C1","Question":"A risk described as “material” is:","A":"physical only","B":"significant enough to matter","C":"already closed","D":"impossible to quantify","Source ID":"D-014"},{"ID":"T1-15","Test":"Simulation 1","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Vocabulary","Level":"C1","Question":"To “ring-fence” a budget means to:","A":"remove it","B":"protect it for a specific purpose","C":"double