ange window remains approved.","C":"Do the needful ASAP.","D":"Kindly revert.","Source ID":"D-022"},{"ID":"T2-03","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which phrase disagrees constructively?","A":"That makes no sense.","B":"I see the rationale; my concern is the untested recovery path.","C":"You are wrong.","D":"We have already decided.","Source ID":"D-023"},{"ID":"T2-04","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which phrase best checks shared understanding?","A":"Are we good?","B":"To confirm, we will pilot in France before the group-wide rollout, correct?","C":"You understood, right?","D":"Anyway, next.","Source ID":"D-024"},{"ID":"T2-05","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which sentence preserves leverage without sounding hostile?","A":"Take it or leave it.","B":"If the liability cap remains unchanged, we would need stronger service credits.","C":"This is unacceptable.","D":"You must comply immediately.","Source ID":"D-025"},{"ID":"T2-06","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Business","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which sentence uses BLUF?","A":"Following several weeks of detailed analysis…","B":"Recommendation: delay go-live by one week to close the critical recovery gap.","C":"There are many things to discuss.","D":"Please see the 18-page report.","Source ID":"D-026"},{"ID":"T2-07","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Business","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which signpost is most natural?","A":"Now I explain next.","B":"Let me turn to the operational impact.","C":"We go in another point.","D":"Concerning about costs…","Source ID":"D-027"},{"ID":"T2-08","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Business","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which sentence calibrates certainty accurately?","A":"This will definitely never fail.","B":"The evidence suggests the exposure is limited, but two assumptions remain untested.","C":"It should be fine.","D":"There is zero risk.","Source ID":"D-028"},{"ID":"T2-09","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Business","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which escalation is strongest and most neutral?","A":"The team messed up again.","B":"The decision is now time-critical: without approval by Friday, the migration date will move.","C":"This is a disaster.","D":"Nobody is answering.","Source ID":"D-029"},{"ID":"T2-10","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Business","Skill":"Business","Level":"C1","Question":"Which version is actionable?","A":"Improve your communication.","B":"In the next update, lead with the decision required and limit background to three bullets.","C":"Be more professional.","D":"This was confusing.","Source ID":"D-030"},{"ID":"T2-11","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"Residual risk is the risk:","A":"before any controls","B":"remaining after controls are applied","C":"owned by the auditor","D":"transferred to every supplier","Source ID":"D-031"},{"ID":"T2-12","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"Containment primarily aims to:","A":"write the final report","B":"limit the spread and impact of an incident","C":"restore every system immediately","D":"attribute the attacker publicly","Source ID":"D-032"},{"ID":"T2-13","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"An attack surface is:","A":"only internet-facing IPs","B":"the set of reachable points an attacker could target","C":"a list of employees","D":"the annual audit scope","Source ID":"D-033"},{"ID":"T2-14","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"The principle of least privilege means granting:","A":"administrator rights by default","B":"only the access required for the task","C":"the same role to everyone","D":"permanent emergency access","Source ID":"D-034"},{"ID":"T2-15","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"Risk acceptance should normally be:","A":"implicit and unlimited","B":"explicit, time-bound and owned at the right level","C":"decided by any engineer","D":"kept outside governance records","Source ID":"D-035"},{"ID":"T2-16","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Precision","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"A false positive is:","A":"a missed malicious event","B":"a benign event incorrectly flagged as malicious","C":"a confirmed incident","D":"a failed backup","Source ID":"D-036"},{"ID":"T2-17","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Precision","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"RTO refers to:","A":"maximum tolerable data loss","B":"target time to restore a service","C":"time between vulnerabilities","D":"audit retention period","Source ID":"D-037"},{"ID":"T2-18","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Precision","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"RPO refers to:","A":"target maximum data loss measured in time","B":"target recovery duration","C":"patch deployment time","D":"incident closure time","Source ID":"D-038"},{"ID":"T2-19","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Precision","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"A compensating control is:","A":"an unrelated policy","B":"an alternative measure that reduces comparable risk","C":"a price discount","D":"an expired certificate","Source ID":"D-039"},{"ID":"T2-20","Test":"Simulation 2","Part":"Precision","Skill":"Cybersecurity","Level":"C1","Question":"“Tamper-evident” means:","A":"impossible to copy","B":"designed to reveal unauthorised alteration","C":"encrypted with any key","D":"stored for one day","Source ID":"D-040"},{"ID":"T3-01","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Horizontal scaling means:","A":"using a faster CPU","B":"adding more instances","C":"increasing disk size only","D":"moving to another region","Source ID":"D-041"},{"ID":"T3-02","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"A multi-AZ design primarily reduces exposure to:","A":"all global failures","B":"the failure of one availability zone","C":"bad application code","D":"weak passwords","Source ID":"D-042"},{"ID":"T3-03","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Rightsizing means:","A":"buying the largest instance","B":"matching resources to actual workload needs","C":"removing monitoring","D":"prepaying every service","Source ID":"D-043"},{"ID":"T3-04","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"The shared responsibility model clarifies:","A":"that the provider owns every control","B":"how security duties are divided between provider and customer","C":"that audits are unnecessary","D":"that data needs no classification","Source ID":"D-044"},{"ID":"T3-05","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Use of English","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Replatforming usually means:","A":"rewriting everything","B":"making limited cloud optimisations without full redesign","C":"keeping the workload unchanged on-premises","D":"retiring the workload","Source ID":"D-045"},{"ID":"T3-06","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Business","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"An egress control governs:","A":"incoming traffic only","B":"outbound traffic","C":"physical entry","D":"backup retention","Source ID":"D-046"},{"ID":"T3-07","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Business","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Data residency concerns:","A":"file naming conventions","B":"where data is stored and processed geographically","C":"only encryption strength","D":"CPU location inside a server","Source ID":"D-047"},{"ID":"T3-08","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Business","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Infrastructure as code improves:","A":"manual variation","B":"repeatability, reviewability and automation","C":"untracked changes","D":"password sharing","Source ID":"D-048"},{"ID":"T3-09","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Business","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"A blast radius is:","A":"the speed of an attack","B":"the maximum scope affected by a failure or change","C":"a firewall rule count","D":"a backup size","Source ID":"D-049"},{"ID":"T3-10","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Business","Skill":"Cloud","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"A landing zone is:","A":"a single virtual machine","B":"a governed cloud foundation for workloads","C":"an airport network","D":"a temporary test account only","Source ID":"D-050"},{"ID":"T3-11","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Writing","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Choose the most concise version.","A":"Due to the fact that the control is not currently operating effectively, there is a possibility of delay.","B":"Because the control is ineffective, delivery may be delayed.","C":"The control, which is a control, might perhaps lead to some delay.","D":"There may potentially be a delay situation.","Source ID":"D-051"},{"ID":"T3-12","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Writing","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Which sentence separates fact from inference?","A":"The attacker definitely stole data.","B":"Logs show 2.4 GB of outbound traffic; whether it contained customer data is still under investigation.","C":"We know what happened.","D":"It looks bad.","Source ID":"D-052"},{"ID":"T3-13","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Writing","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Best subject line?","A":"Update","B":"Urgent!!!","C":"Decision required by 12 Aug — EU logging retention","D":"Hello about the project","Source ID":"D-053"},{"ID":"T3-14","Test":"Simulation 3","Part":"Cyber & Cloud","Skill":"Writing","Level":"C1–C2","Question":"Best structured risk statement?","A":"Security is bad.","B":"Because privileged accounts lack MFA, credential theft could lead to unauthorised access and material disruption.","C":"We need MF